        "",
        "## 3. Automation Strategy",
        "",
        f"- **Framework:** {project_config.get('automation', {}).get('framework', 'Not specified')} (declared in project adapter).",
        f"- **Language:** {project_config.get('automation', {}).get('language', 'Not specified')} (declared in project adapter).",
        "- **Approach:** Page Object Model for UI tests. API client for API tests. Fixtures for test data setup.",
        "- **Test organization:** One test file per acceptance criterion, with shared fixtures for test data and environment setup.",
        "",
        "## 4. Test Data Strategy",
        "",
        "- **Precondition entities:** Any pre-existing entities required by the acceptance criteria (e.g., registered users, existing orders, configured settings). These should be created via seed scripts, API calls, or database fixtures before tests run.",
        "- **Invalid input samples:** Invalid inputs required to test negative scenarios. Includes invalid credentials, malformed data, out-of-range values.",
        "- **Boundary values:** Very long strings, whitespace-only strings, special character strings, empty values, maximum/minimum values for relevant fields.",
        "",
        "## 5. Environment Strategy",
        "",
    ]

    if env_enabled:
        arch_lines.extend([
            "- **Target environment:** Dev or staging (as enabled in project adapter).",
            "- **Environment isolation:** Tests should run against an isolated environment to avoid affecting production data or other testers.",
            "- **Environment cleanup:** Tests should clean up any data they create (e.g., sessions, test users) after execution.",
        ])
    else:
        arch_lines.extend([
            "- **Target environment:** NONE — No dev, staging, or production environment is enabled in the project adapter. This is a hard blocker for test execution.",
            "- **Environment isolation:** Not applicable — no environment available.",
            "- **Environment cleanup:** Not applicable — no environment available.",
            "",
            "## 5a. Environment Blocker",
            "",
            "***BLOCKED:** No environments are enabled in the project adapter (environments.dev=false, staging=false, production=false). Test execution cannot proceed until at least a test environment is configured. This blocks Stages 10-14 (Execution through Final Report).*",
            "",
        ])

    arch_lines.extend([
        "## 6. Mocking Strategy",
        "",
        "- **External dependencies:** If the feature depends on external services (SSO, email verification, third-party identity providers, payment gateways), these should be mocked or stubbed in test environments.",
        "- **API responses:** API tests may mock downstream service responses to isolate the feature endpoint behavior.",
        "",
        "## 7. CI Strategy",
        "",
        f"- **CI provider:** {project_config.get('ci', {}).get('provider', 'None declared')}.",
        "- **Run trigger:** On pull requests and merges to main, run the feature test suite.",
        "- **Reporting:** Test results should be reported to the CI pipeline with pass/fail summary and evidence links.",
        "",
        "## 8. Reporting Strategy",
        "",
        "- **Test results:** Pass/fail for each acceptance criterion and scenario.",
        "- **Evidence:** Screenshots for UI test failures, API response logs for API test failures, console logs for JavaScript errors.",
        "- **Coverage:** Statement coverage for unit tests (if applicable), scenario coverage for integration and E2E tests.",
        "",
        "## 9. Risks",
